!! 1. TiddlyFlashcards

> ''Write your understanding into tiddlers.''
> ''Create flashcards worth remembering.''
> ''Use Anki to review.''

TiddlyFlashcards is more than just a plugin. It's a workflow that connects TiddlyWiki with Anki, making it easier to turn understanding into long-term memory.

Rather than replacing either tool, TiddlyFlashcards combines their strengths in a single learning workflow.

|tc-max-width|k
| !Component | !Main responsibility |
|TiddlyWiki |Knowledge authoring and organization (flashcards stay in context) |
|TiddlyFlashcards |Focused flashcard creation and synchronization |
|Anki |Spaced repetition and review |

The idea is simple: separate note-taking from flashcard creation, but keep the two connected.

